  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1...Chances for showers and thunderstorms will continue \nthrough the end of the week and into the weekend. Any thunderstorms \nthat do form my be capable of producing locally heavy downpours\nand gusty winds.\n\nA few showers will continue to work through the region overnight but \nmost areas will see largely dry weather through the early morning \nhours. There will also be the potential for some fog, mainly \nacross the S. Tier and in the river valleys. \n\nAfter sunrise...any fog that is around will quickly dissipate with \nanother warm and humid day (dewpoints in the mid/upper 60s to around \n70F). Highs again will climb firmly into the 80s, with even some \nlocations approaching 90F. Heat index values will again range from \nthe upper 80s to low 90s in the warmest locations.  \n\nShowers and thunderstorm coverage will remain fairly sparse across \nfar western New York this afternoon. Even guidance suggests that PW \nvalues will fall off into the 1.2\" to 1.4\" range as drier air works \ninto the mid-levels. The further east you go it will be a bit of a \ndifferent story, largely from the Genesee Valley east across the \nFinger Lakes region and northeast into the North Country inland\naway from Lake Ontario. This is where deeper moisture (PW \nvalues +1.7) will be found, MLCAPE +2K, and somewhat better \nsupport aloft this afternoon and evening. Also...0-6km shear \nvalues of 25-35 knots may support a few storms to become strong \nenough to produce strong gusty winds. However...the main threat \nwill 'likely' be localized heavy rainfall. WPC continues to \nadvertise all of the region in a marginal risk for excessive \nrainfall given the overall high PW values. \n\nThe mid-level trough and cold front slowly inch east towards the \nregion Friday, with a better chance for widespread showers and \nthunderstorms in the afternoon. Moisture will again tick up with PW \nvalues of +1.7\" across the region and MLCAPE values north of +2K \ninland from the lakes. Guidance suggest we might even see a convectively\naugmented shortwave move through the region just before or \naround peak heating. We will need to keep an eye on this \nfeature as it may aid in the severe wx potential Friday. \n\nFriday night and Saturday...we will see addtional chances for showers \nand thunderstorms as cold front nears and then eventually crosses \nthe region. \n\nKey Message 2...Brief reprieve from the showers and \nthunderstorms Sunday, then unsettle weather returns Monday and \nTuesday. \n\nIt looks like we will see drier, cooler, and less humid conditions \nSunday behind the passage of the cold front. That said...it doesn't \nlast long as chances for showers and thunderstorms return \nMonday. We will also see a warming trend with humidity \nreturning which looks like it will be with us through atleast \nTuesday.",
